================================================================================
PATH 1b increment 4b: MPI-parallelise the O(N^2) FPOLY0 initial force build
================================================================================
Date     : 2026-06-07
Branch   : mpi-parallel
Binary   : GPU2/run_versions/nbody7b.mpi-cpu  (pure-MPI, OMP_NUM_THREADS=1)
Harness  : mpi_design/poc_validation/scale_split.py  (min-of-2, np={1,2,4,8})
Inputs   : input_gen_N13049_eq , input_gen_N50000_eq  (equal-mass generated Plummer)

WHAT CHANGED  (builds on increment 4 = FPOLY2 startup, commit bf84510)
  GPU2/fpoly0.f        : the one-shot initial force/neighbour build (the
                         NIMAX-block loop calling GPUNB_REGF + GPUIRR_FIRR_VEC
                         over all IFIRST..NTOT) is now MPI-split. FPOLY0 is
                         EMBARRASSINGLY PARALLEL in the particle index -- each
                         particle's force depends only on the fully-replicated
                         j-particle state (GPUNB_SEND / GPUIRR_SET_JP send ALL
                         particles on every rank) with NO cross-particle
                         ordering (unlike FPOLY2's STEPS F/FDOT scaling). So
                         each rank runs the block loop over its own contiguous
                         slice [MYP0..MYP0+MYNP-1] (via the existing
                         NBODY_REGF_RANGE) and the per-particle results are
                         Allgathered. The replicated XTRNLD + F/FDOT/D0/D0R/
                         FIDOT/FRDOT assembly that follows runs on identical
                         gathered inputs. NRANKS=1 -> original serial loop.
  GPU2/mpi_nbody.f     : + NBODY_FPOLY0_GATHER (6 Allgatherv).
  GPU2/mpi_nbody_stub.f: + no-op stub (serial / AMUSE builds unchanged).

GATHER SET (per particle, over [IFIRST,NTOT]):
  FR,D1R (regular force+deriv), FI,D1 (irregular force+deriv)  -- (3,*)
  RS (neighbour radius; the overflow branch may adjust it per particle) -- (1,*)
  LIST (integer neighbour lists, LMAX column stride)           -- (LMAX,*)
  (F,FDOT,D0,D0R,FIDOT,FRDOT are formed replicated AFTER the gather from these.)

KEY RESULT: bit-identical to single-rank serial np=1/2/4/8 at both N, and the
O(N^2) FPOLY0 startup -- the dominant remaining startup floor after FPOLY2 --
now parallelises, taking raw in-code wall close to the integration ceiling.

