STARTUP PROGRESSION at N=50000, np8 (each step removes one O(N^2) serial piece):
  pre-startup-decomp (HEAD pre-bf84510) : 43s  (ROSE with np; replicated FPOLY0+FPOLY2)
  + FPOLY2 decomposed (bf84510)         : 31s  (FPOLY2 share removed; FPOLY0 floor)
  + FPOLY0 decomposed (this increment)  : 12s  (38->12 = 3.2x; ~78% parallel)
RAW in-code wall np8 speedup at N=50000: 1.66x -> 2.04x (FPOLY2) -> 3.43x (FPOLY0),
now near the integration-only ceiling (3.62x). Integration speedup unchanged
(np8 3.62-3.73x, p~0.83-0.85) -- the integration path is untouched.

REMAINING ~12s startup floor at np8 = the still-serial parts of START outside the
two force builds: INPUT/DATA/SCALE (IC generation), GPUNB_OPEN/SEND + GPUIRR setup
(replicated by design -- every rank needs the full j-state), KSPINIT, and the
replicated XTRNLD/assembly post-loops. These are O(N) or setup-bound, not O(N^2),
so the dominant large-N startup cost is now addressed. Further trimming (rank-0
I/O, overlap) is lower-yield -- see the integration-serial-trim lever (Path 2).
